WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.456 --> 00:00:03.206
(dramatic music)

00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:14.910
- Hey everyone, my name is Jesse

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.030
and today, I'm gonna be testing out

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.820
five famous celebrity omelet recipes,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.710
to see which one is actually the best.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.850
Today, I'm gonna be testing recipes

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.020
from Emeril Lagasse, Julia
Child, Geoffrey Zakarian,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.600
Masaharu Morimoto and LL Cool J.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.460
I studied up on all their techniques,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.440
weighed all the ingredients
to level the playing field

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.960
and I got three of my
friends to taste them

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.020
in a blind taste test.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.180
So, which celebrity chef
has the best omelet?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.423
Let's start the eggs-periment.

00:00:36.423 --> 00:00:37.256
(chicken bawking)

00:00:37.256 --> 00:00:40.360
Emeril Lagasse starts by
placing some eggs, heavy cream,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.190
salt and white pepper in a
blender and then blitzes that up

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.780
until it's nice and frothy,
so about 60 seconds.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.140
Then he puts some melted butter

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.890
and puts the egg mixture
in a heated skillet

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.500
and pushes it around
with a rubber spatula,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.260
kind of like you're making scrambled eggs.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.730
This is just to get it
to cook evenly all over.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:57.170
Then he takes his spatula, and
kind of smooths out the top

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.120
to make sure it's an
even depth throughout,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.890
puts some shredded cheddar cheese on top

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.610
and folds it into a half moon shape,

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.200
transfers that onto a plate, and bam!

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.310
Even more cheese.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.010
- You see eggs and cheese all the time.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.360
It's like peanut butter and jelly.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.460
- I definitely like the coloration of it.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.700
- Look how thick that is.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.537
- I'm gonna go ahead and get into it.

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:16.202
(cheerful music)

00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:17.143
- Mm.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.340
- Ah, it's just some regular eggs.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.350
- Cheese is nicely melted,
the eggs are cooked great.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.430
This is a good omelet.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:23.290
- I don't know who made that one

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.040
but tastes like I made it.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.140
- It's really good.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.840
I'm actually gonna finish this.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.673
Mm.

00:01:28.673 --> 00:01:30.920
- [Jesse Voiceover] Up next is
legendary chef, Julia Child.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.730
She starts with two eggs,
some salt and pepper

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.930
and blends those together
with some chopsticks.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.390
She adds a little bit of water to 'em

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.496
and also says you can use a whisk

00:01:38.496 --> 00:01:41.280
and goes back and forth, so I did too.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.260
Then she heats some butter in a skillet

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.150
and then adds the egg mixture to that,

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.690
and this is where it gets cool.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:47.880
You just swirl, swirl, swirl

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.590
and it manageably turns into an omelet.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.790
You barely have to touch it.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.940
You can kind of piece it together

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.850
with the chopsticks, but that's about it.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.550
Then she rubs some butter on top,

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.880
garnish it with parsley and bon appetit.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.429
- This looks like a fancy omelet.

00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:00.613
- Damn. That's thick.

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:02.380
(cheerful music)

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.680
- It's softer.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.290
I like the texture a lot.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.123
- I do like it.

00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:08.730
But this is just very fresh and light,

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.650
and I'm going to eat this with my pinky up

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.500
because that's what this tastes like.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.480
Tastes way better with your pinky up.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.350
- [Jesse Voiceover] Up
next is Geoffrey Zakarian.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.280
He starts with three eggs and
adds a extra egg yolk to them

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.300
to give it a nice, rich quality.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.780
Then he adds diced, frozen
butter to it, and mixes that in.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.350
He adds that to a pan, slowly heats it up

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.960
so the butter melts throughout
and it gets nice and creamy,

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.246
kind of like you're
making soft scrambled eggs

00:02:33.246 --> 00:02:35.598
and then lets it set for a second.

00:02:35.598 --> 00:02:37.936
He seasons the top with salt and pepper

00:02:37.936 --> 00:02:40.390
and puts shredded Gruyere cheese

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.280
and chopped fresh herbs on top.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.470
He rolls that up with a
spatula, transfers it to a plate

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.950
and then garnishes it
with extra chopped herbs

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.760
and even more cheese to
make it look nice and fancy.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:51.776
- This omelet right here looks

00:02:51.776 --> 00:02:53.530
really freaking good, alright?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.650
I like the artistry.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.120
I like the yellows with
the whites with the greens.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.810
- I'm seeing cheese
but I think I can smell

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.470
that it's Parmesan cheese.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.270
- This looks like a cinnamon roll.

00:03:05.279 --> 00:03:06.710
I don't know, it's not doing much for me.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.630
The texture's okay,
it's a little too solid.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.810
- This person definitely
has different taste buds.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.680
- I wish it was more
scrambled or more creamy.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.460
- It's a little bit of an herb overload.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.780
- If you're into very
stinky kinda funky cheeses,

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.210
then you'll be into this omelet.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.900
I'm not into stinky funky cheeses,

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.340
so I ain't into this omelet.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.495
I like the way it looks, but
not the way it tastes, boo boo.

00:03:26.495 --> 00:03:28.430
- [Jesse Voiceover] Iron
Chef Morimoto starts

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.620
by adding sugar, light soy
sauce, and dashi in a bowl

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.660
and stirring it together
to dissolve the sugar.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.500
And adds four eggs to that.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.320
He mixes those in to
create one cohesive mixture

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.430
and then strains that into another bowl.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.140
Oil a pan with a rolled paper towel

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.060
and adds some of the egg mixture to it.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.160
It might puff up a bit, so
just pop any of the bubbles

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.000
with your chopsticks and push
them all towards the front,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.553
as if you're rolling a carpet.

00:03:50.553 --> 00:03:52.310
(dramatic music)

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.450
Oil it up one more time
and add a bit more eggs.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.040
Make sure to get underneath the first roll

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.790
so it kind of glues together a bit.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.440
You're gonna have to do
this three more times

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.990
until it's one large roll.

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.690
At this point, just transfer
to a plate and that's it.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.700
- Never seen an omelet this color,

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.990
but it looks like it's not
gonna have any flavor to it

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.880
because there is no ingredients
other than the egg on it.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.710
- Visually, it's a no for me.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:17.830
- This looks sweet.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.250
It like sparkles.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.270
- The roll is really perfect.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.103
Look at that roll.

00:04:21.103 --> 00:04:22.550
- It doesn't look like
there's anything in it.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:27.275
It's just an egg over
and over and over again.

00:04:27.275 --> 00:04:28.630
- Mm.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.290
- I don't even know what
I'm tasting right now.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.330
- I really like this.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.990
There's definitely
something sweet about it.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.080
- I don't think there's enough
happening for me to like it.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.310
It's a thumbs down.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.143
- I like this.

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:38.976
I'm feeling this.

00:04:38.976 --> 00:04:42.190
- Half of the food eating
experience is aesthetics

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.032
so I dig this.

00:04:44.032 --> 00:04:45.570
- [Jesse Voiceover] LL
Cool J starts by separating

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.760
a whopping nine egg
whites from their yolks.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.620
He sprays a pan with non-stick spray,

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.420
adds diced yellow and red peppers

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.061
and cooks those until tender.

00:04:54.061 --> 00:04:55.760
You're gonna wanna
break up your egg whites

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.940
just a little bit so they're
not all stuck together.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.460
Add some spinach to the
pan, salt and pepper

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.950
and let the spinach wilt
so it gets nice and tender.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.640
Add your egg whites back to the pan

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.303
and push them around
with your rubber spatula

00:05:06.303 --> 00:05:08.690
a little bit to help them cook evenly.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.220
Season again with salt and pepper

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.540
and let 'em cook up so they
set all the way on the bottom.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.880
Fold it in half into a half moon shape,

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.170
transfer it onto a plate and that's it.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.560
Turns out nine egg yolks is how

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.952
a 50 year-old stays so ripped.

00:05:20.952 --> 00:05:21.785
- Whoa!

00:05:21.785 --> 00:05:23.720
Egg whites, are we healthy or nah?

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.220
- Lot of vegetables happening.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.000
It's important to get your vitamins.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.540
- I mean it's eggs, so
how bad could it be?

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.200
Mm hm.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.240
Pretty bad, yeah.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.850
- It tastes way too
healthy, like something

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.370
